A||N||3||Shadow||Timing way off but running??? Help||||9||
Z||000000||Shadow||04-06-2001||02:29 AM||||Let me bring everyone up to speed.  My engine blew out back in December.  I went to a local shop that I knew used to be good and it took them about a month to get a replacement into the car (another 2.8L).  They broken the old harmonic balancer so they got me a new one.  I ended up replacing the stock coil with the one from accel, a couple of days later it fried my distributor (so the shop said) I went to the Local part store and got a reman one and had the shop put it in...<BR>OK here is my problem, the car was surging as soon as I would hit the gas and while cruising.  I checked the timing, It was way off so I moved it back to 10 degrees and the car dies, it will not run for more than 3 seconds.  I moved the timing back to where the shop had it and it is running again, here is the thing doing a little eye-balling I would say the timing is about 20~25 degrees advanced.  Whats going on?<BR>My though right now is that the balancer that the shop got for me is not the right one or that the distributor is way off.<BR>Any thoughts? ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Wolfhound||04-06-2001||07:14 AM||||My guess is the harmonic balancer is for another engine application that had the scale positioned differently.<BR>I suggest locating TDC manually and see what you come up with. You may have to make your own mark.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-06-2001||11:25 AM||||The Timing marks are not in the same location on a FWD 2.8L engine but the balancer will fit both engines. I would follow Wolfhounds Idea. Find TDC of the #1 piston then paint a white line at "0*" on the balancer then recheck the timing.<BR>If the timing mark does line up with TDC, they may be one tooth off on the timing chain between the cam and crankshaft.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||thrax82||04-06-2001||11:43 AM||||go to the pick in pull and find a mid mounted fiero like yours with the v 6 and ether pull that one off or take your other one with you line them both up and mark were the other harmonic balencers timming mark is<BR>and when you do the timming make sure you put the computer in dianostic mode other wise it will move the disstributor when you do ||||reg||4
